WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
Safex

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:09.633
Candy did her best to take care
of the girl in the Special-Care ward.

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:13.040
The girl was healed from
her psychological problem.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.479
Candy received her Thank-You letter.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:19.009
Her hard work paid off.

00:00:19.159 --> 00:00:22.179
A sense of duty for being
a nurse arised in her heart.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:31.087
Rumours about Terrius.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.331
It's going to be hotter after the rain
isn't it?

00:00:40.481 --> 00:00:41.702
Silly girl!

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:43.975
Yes, Principal!

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:48.672
Your letter and package.

00:00:48.822 --> 00:00:50.337
Thanks.

00:00:50.487 --> 00:00:53.078
You receive many letters lately.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:05.691
Stear and Archie have been very sweet to me
since they returned to America.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:08.656
It must be very tiring being a nurse.

00:01:08.806 --> 00:01:11.202
A little treat for you.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.436
What did they give me?

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.571
Candy!

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.289
Everyone!

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:35.889
Everyone, have one of these.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.298
- So beautiful!
- Nice candy!

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.463
They are from my friend.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.700
Must be your boyfriend.

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:48.472
Thanks.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.478
- Let's eat!
- Please.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.178
Have more.

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:56.546
So tasty!

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.720
Do you want some, Franny?

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:04.785
They are a gift from my friend.

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:06.582
I don't want any.

00:02:06.732 --> 00:02:09.059
Don't be shy, please.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:13.324
Candy, I told you before.

00:02:13.474 --> 00:02:15.799
I hate people who talk too much.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.796
Do you really understand what I said?

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:25.638
Honestly, I hate people like you.

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:35.377
Franny, why did you say that?

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:36.950
That's true.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:45.129
This is my first time

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.899
to be criticized like this.

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:08.087
I don't know how much she hates me.

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.789
I'd better be quiet.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.885
Did you hear that?
Something terrible happened!

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.462
The Austrian Prince was murdered!

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.922
By a Serbian man?

00:03:22.072 --> 00:03:26.301
Things are complicating.
I hope the war won't start.

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:34.103
Bad news came one after another.

00:03:34.253 --> 00:03:37.205
Dark clouds are everywhere.

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:01.230
Finally the sky got clearer.

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:04.871
The sun is brighter and brighter.

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:09.478
I want to go swimming in the lake
when the weather is a little bit nicer.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.715
Annie, Archie, Stear.

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:18.618
I wish Patty was here too!

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.959
Sister Candy!

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:25.689
What are you thinking about,
sister Candy?

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:31.164
Something must be bothering you, otherwise
you wouldn't stare out of the window.

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:33.893
It's nothing!

00:04:34.043 --> 00:04:35.461
Then what are you doing?

00:04:35.611 --> 00:04:37.065
I am sunbathing.

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:42.046
Please don't tell headmistress Merry Jane.

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:46.305
Only if you give us some drawing books.
It's too boring.

00:04:46.455 --> 00:04:48.143
- Me, too!
- Alright.

00:04:48.293 --> 00:04:51.913
I'll go get some during the break time.
You guys behave yourselves!

00:04:52.063 --> 00:04:53.320
Ok!

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:09.431
We stay in the hospital all day.

00:05:09.581 --> 00:05:12.067
There are so many exciting things
happening downtown!

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:20.884
Grandpa, do you sell drawing books here?

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:24.550
There seems to be a couple.

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:27.287
Here?

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:38.396
This is....

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:43.665
Terry.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.432
"A hopeful new star appears!"

00:05:46.582 --> 00:05:50.640
"Terrius in a Shakespeare play.
A new star on Broadway!"

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:56.284
Terry!

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:58.756
I finally found you!

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:17.800
Terry, how are you?
You became so mature!

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:21.345
I miss you so much!

00:06:25.218 --> 00:06:29.245
Broadway...
Terry became an actor!

00:06:30.757 --> 00:06:32.548
Last summer....

00:06:32.698 --> 00:06:36.685
It was the first time he talked about drama
in the Scottish summer school.

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:39.989
Shakespeare.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:43.557
This is your book.
You like dramas, Terry?

00:06:43.707 --> 00:06:45.360
- No.
- Liar!

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:48.262
There are notes everywhere in your book.

00:06:48.412 --> 00:06:49.567
You still want to deny it?

00:06:49.717 --> 00:06:53.110
Truth is I do like dramas, a lot.

00:06:58.451 --> 00:07:03.081
Terry was so devoted back then.

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:04.822
Terry.

00:07:05.191 --> 00:07:07.284
In order to be able to see you....

00:07:10.797 --> 00:07:13.493
I took the carriage chasing you all night.

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:20.301
The boat was sailing away
in the first ray of the morning sun.

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:25.401
The sound of the steam whistle
came from the distance.

00:07:25.551 --> 00:07:27.837
As long as we stay alive,
we will meet again someday.

00:07:27.987 --> 00:07:29.871
Because of this sentence.

00:07:30.021 --> 00:07:33.277
It has been half of a year...

00:07:37.557 --> 00:07:40.321
...since I saw the boat going away
in the first ray of the morning sun.

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:45.837
I chose to be a nurse.

00:07:45.987 --> 00:07:49.196
You headed towards
the entertainment business.

00:07:50.336 --> 00:07:53.737
You are now in New York.

00:08:06.853 --> 00:08:08.343
Who is it?

00:08:09.155 --> 00:08:10.486
What's your name?

00:08:11.657 --> 00:08:13.916
Don't be afraid if I tell you.

00:08:14.066 --> 00:08:18.152
It won't happen.
I am not even afraid of hell!

00:08:18.302 --> 00:08:20.724
My name is Macbeth.

00:08:22.702 --> 00:08:25.762
Devil!
Do not speak such a dirty name!

00:08:25.912 --> 00:08:29.264
Hearing my name does make you afraid.

00:08:29.414 --> 00:08:32.344
You are lying!
Macbeth is a cursed name!

00:08:33.579 --> 00:08:36.742
Let me cut your delusion with my sword!

00:08:56.569 --> 00:08:59.160
Special edition!

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:02.397
Special edition!

00:09:09.315 --> 00:09:12.738
His Majesty is still a minor.
He doesn't deserve to die.

00:09:12.888 --> 00:09:16.347
The evil Macbeth stole his soul.

00:09:16.497 --> 00:09:18.949
Is he dead?

00:09:19.325 --> 00:09:21.486
Long live His Majesty!

00:09:22.461 --> 00:09:25.406
Good news, look!

00:09:25.556 --> 00:09:27.999
The man who made us suffer
was decapitated.

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:30.998
We are free!

00:09:31.337 --> 00:09:36.969
Scotland! Hooray!

00:09:44.517 --> 00:09:46.640
Special edition!

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:48.875
The war started!

00:09:49.025 --> 00:09:51.455
Special edition! The war started!

00:09:53.426 --> 00:09:56.520
Special edition!

00:09:57.296 --> 00:09:58.854
Special edition !

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:03.757
The war between Austria and Serbia started!

00:10:03.907 --> 00:10:06.770
Special edition !

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:09.007
Hurry!

00:10:14.347 --> 00:10:15.974
War?

00:10:18.784 --> 00:10:21.514
The war between Austria and Serbia started!

00:10:40.706 --> 00:10:43.133
Special edition!

00:10:43.283 --> 00:10:45.676
The war started!

00:10:48.314 --> 00:10:50.214
It has nothing to do with America.

00:10:50.416 --> 00:10:52.145
It's awful! Let me see!

00:11:00.726 --> 00:11:03.524
How will the troupe survive
if the war started?

00:11:04.263 --> 00:11:06.557
There might be fewer shows.

00:11:06.733 --> 00:11:09.674
What are we going to do with our jobs?

00:11:09.824 --> 00:11:11.729
Things will find their ways.

00:11:11.879 --> 00:11:13.805
I have nothing to do with this.

00:11:14.073 --> 00:11:16.373
Everyone, did you read
the morning newspaper?

00:11:17.309 --> 00:11:21.334
Look! Terrius's photo!

00:11:21.584 --> 00:11:22.998
- Terrius?
- Where?

00:11:23.182 --> 00:11:25.041
A new man with bright future.

00:11:25.685 --> 00:11:29.387
Skilful and eye-catching acting.

00:11:30.089 --> 00:11:33.752
A new man worthy of great expectation.

00:11:45.271 --> 00:11:47.062
Terrius, did you read the newspaper?

00:11:47.212 --> 00:11:48.561
Yes, I did.

00:11:48.711 --> 00:11:52.037
You received good reviews.
And a photo, too!

00:11:54.547 --> 00:11:56.678
Everybody is looking forward to you.

00:11:56.949 --> 00:11:59.309
A rising shiny star.

00:11:59.459 --> 00:12:01.818
Thanks. Excuse me.

00:12:05.624 --> 00:12:07.450
He is too arrogant.

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:08.885
Excuse me.

00:12:09.035 --> 00:12:11.189
He is too new to be so arrogant.

00:12:12.998 --> 00:12:15.190
He is so handsome!

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:19.431
True. Young and good at acting.
Unlimited future.

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:23.231
I am so sad!

00:12:28.981 --> 00:12:32.883
The war is going to affect America anytime.

00:12:33.552 --> 00:12:34.917
Candy.

00:12:38.324 --> 00:12:42.522
Are you still in England?

00:12:42.762 --> 00:12:45.754
I really hope that
I can cross the ocean to find Candy.

00:12:47.833 --> 00:12:50.097
The St. Paul Academy in London.

00:12:53.839 --> 00:12:56.501
Those memorable days won't come back again.

00:13:22.868 --> 00:13:24.733
Mr. Terrius!

00:13:25.738 --> 00:13:26.928
Mr. Terrius!

00:13:27.078 --> 00:13:29.832
Warrick Troupe in New York
wants to have an interview with you.

00:13:29.982 --> 00:13:31.534
I'll go right away.

00:13:33.345 --> 00:13:36.605
Candy, I am already
in the entertainment business.

00:13:36.755 --> 00:13:38.410
I can't go back.

00:13:38.651 --> 00:13:42.087
When will we meet again?
God bless England.

00:13:52.598 --> 00:13:55.587
The rumour finally came true.

00:13:55.737 --> 00:13:58.527
We will get involved sooner or later.

00:13:58.677 --> 00:14:01.663
America will join the war then.

00:14:09.582 --> 00:14:12.206
The whole city is talking about the war.

00:14:12.356 --> 00:14:14.474
However, the patients here
are still relaxed.

00:14:14.624 --> 00:14:17.318
The hospital won't be affected.

00:14:26.832 --> 00:14:29.223
Candice, where are you going?

00:14:29.373 --> 00:14:31.858
Excuse me. Anything wrong?

00:14:32.008 --> 00:14:36.533
Headmistress Merry Jane wants everyone
to gather in the Principal's Office.

00:14:36.683 --> 00:14:38.439
The headmistress?

00:14:39.011 --> 00:14:40.342
Go!

00:14:46.652 --> 00:14:49.579
Big news! You heard about that?

00:14:49.829 --> 00:14:54.079
Don't mention the war
in front of the patients!

00:14:54.229 --> 00:14:58.424
So that the patients will not be anxious.

00:14:59.265 --> 00:15:02.262
Please be aware of that.

00:15:07.239 --> 00:15:08.328
Also,

00:15:08.478 --> 00:15:11.967
there will be an important
matter announced soon.

00:15:12.711 --> 00:15:15.071
You have to stay calm.

00:15:15.221 --> 00:15:16.379
Yes.

00:15:17.349 --> 00:15:18.748
Dismissed.

00:15:26.025 --> 00:15:28.084
What important matter?

00:15:29.895 --> 00:15:32.728
What's the school going to do
once we join the war?

00:15:33.766 --> 00:15:37.293
Everyone, watch your conversation.

00:15:38.437 --> 00:15:40.161
That's Franny.

00:15:40.311 --> 00:15:42.506
Assertive like headmistress Merry Jane.

00:15:54.053 --> 00:15:56.278
What a beautiful sunset!

00:15:56.428 --> 00:15:58.720
What happened today was so unreal.

00:15:58.991 --> 00:16:00.884
But it was real.

00:16:01.034 --> 00:16:02.722
This news.

00:16:03.062 --> 00:16:05.326
And the war.

00:16:22.381 --> 00:16:26.613
Bad news!
England declared war to Germany!

00:16:27.052 --> 00:16:28.445
England?

00:16:28.595 --> 00:16:31.076
This way, America....

00:16:31.226 --> 00:16:34.084
Finally England was involved in the war.

00:16:34.234 --> 00:16:36.423
Patty is still in England.

00:16:40.566 --> 00:16:42.431
Will Patty be alright?

00:16:42.634 --> 00:16:45.432
Stear must be worried.

00:16:46.138 --> 00:16:48.766
Sister!

00:16:49.942 --> 00:16:51.842
Sister Candy!

00:16:54.313 --> 00:16:56.971
You promised you would bring me
a drawing book.

00:16:57.121 --> 00:16:59.073
You didn't keep your promise!

00:16:59.818 --> 00:17:01.211
Sorry!

00:17:01.361 --> 00:17:06.417
I can't make the patients anxious.
I have to be more cheerful.

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:11.387
I am good at telling stories.

00:17:11.537 --> 00:17:14.125
Sit down.

00:17:18.871 --> 00:17:20.202
Doctor Frank.

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:25.200
What is it?
Did silly girl get lazy again?

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:27.941
Don't worry, Principal.

00:17:28.147 --> 00:17:29.614
She is there.

00:17:32.484 --> 00:17:35.749
The big wolf could only....

00:17:38.557 --> 00:17:42.088
Cheerful as usual.

00:17:43.495 --> 00:17:47.991
We need more nurses like her.

00:17:55.607 --> 00:17:57.268
No, Mr. Daniel!

00:17:57.543 --> 00:18:00.736
Doctor Frank said
that you are not allowed to move yet.

00:18:00.936 --> 00:18:04.204
But, I want to go back to work.

00:18:04.454 --> 00:18:08.609
I know. Please bear with it
for a little longer.

00:18:09.555 --> 00:18:10.954
Mr. Daniel!

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:13.104
How come you are here?

00:18:14.026 --> 00:18:15.584
I....

00:18:16.395 --> 00:18:20.331
Candy, he is not allowed to walk around.
Didn't you know that?

00:18:21.967 --> 00:18:24.192
It's not hurting anymore.

00:18:24.342 --> 00:18:27.898
You don't care
if you will be a cripple forever?

00:18:29.975 --> 00:18:32.836
Franny, he is just trying
to walk a little bit.

00:18:32.986 --> 00:18:34.568
It's not that serious.

00:18:34.718 --> 00:18:36.939
You are not sensitive enough.

00:18:37.089 --> 00:18:41.179
Our carelessness can make
the patients' problems more serious.

00:18:41.453 --> 00:18:43.644
It is a good thing
that the patients like you,

00:18:43.794 --> 00:18:45.648
but you still need to work hard.

00:18:45.798 --> 00:18:46.951
Yes.

00:18:48.694 --> 00:18:50.992
Right...
The headmistress is looking for you.

00:18:52.598 --> 00:18:54.025
Franny.

00:18:54.199 --> 00:18:55.989
Sorry, Candy.

00:18:56.139 --> 00:18:59.502
That's alright. Let me walk
you back to the room.

00:19:06.712 --> 00:19:08.236
Franny Hamilton,

00:19:08.914 --> 00:19:10.176
Judy Netz,

00:19:10.549 --> 00:19:12.073
Natalie Beans,

00:19:12.384 --> 00:19:13.872
Eleanor Munsey,

00:19:14.022 --> 00:19:15.440
Candice White.

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:16.987
Yes!

00:19:17.623 --> 00:19:19.750
No need to answer.

00:19:22.528 --> 00:19:26.790
The above people will be sent
at St. Joanna Hospital, in Chicago.

00:19:27.733 --> 00:19:29.291
Chicago?

00:19:37.376 --> 00:19:41.435
St. Joanna Hospital
is our headquarters.

00:19:41.585 --> 00:19:46.211
The surgical department is
the best among its field.

00:19:46.618 --> 00:19:49.979
Stear, Archie, Annie
are all in Chicago.

00:19:50.129 --> 00:19:54.957
Learn the surgical skill well
and become outstanding nurses.

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:57.051
Surgical skill? But why?

00:19:57.201 --> 00:19:59.089
Must be for the war.

00:19:59.239 --> 00:20:00.932
Are they war nurses?

00:20:01.133 --> 00:20:03.392
War nurses?

00:20:06.505 --> 00:20:11.169
Going to the cruel battlefield
to take care of the wounded soldiers.

00:20:17.249 --> 00:20:22.448
It's true
that we might become the war nurses.

00:20:26.158 --> 00:20:29.817
America is ready to join the war.

00:20:29.967 --> 00:20:32.829
How about Terry's
entertainment business?

00:20:33.098 --> 00:20:36.951
Headmistress,
America won't join the war, right?

00:20:39.071 --> 00:20:40.463
Quiet!

00:20:40.613 --> 00:20:43.473
There are no nationalities
in medical treatment!

00:20:45.944 --> 00:20:49.175
Care should be fairly
provided to everyone.

00:20:49.781 --> 00:20:53.676
It has nothing to do
with countries or races.

00:20:53.826 --> 00:20:56.515
Everyone is equal.

00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:01.088
Everyone is equal.

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:03.123
Great saying!

00:21:06.732 --> 00:21:12.364
Candy's heart is echoing
with what headmistress Merry Jane said.

00:21:13.105 --> 00:21:18.133
She decided to go to Chicago
to learn the surgical skill.

00:21:18.377 --> 00:21:20.868
Candy is waiting for that moment.
